  <!-- EN: legacy ballistic missile body -->
  <DMSE_MissileBody_LegacyBallistic.label>TODO</DMSE_MissileBody_LegacyBallistic.label>
  <!-- EN: A first-generation ballistic rocket in the mould of the V-2: a liquid-fuelled airframe with a mechanical inertial platform and radio lateral correction and no true terminal guidance, slow to prepare and wildly inaccurate by modern standards, devoting most of its mass to structure and propellant but able to be assembled in a silo out of industrial stock long before real strategic systems exist. -->
  <DMSE_MissileBody_LegacyBallistic.description>TODO</DMSE_MissileBody_LegacyBallistic.description>
  <!-- EN: legacy loitering munition -->
  <DMSE_MissileBody_LegacyLoiter.label>TODO</DMSE_MissileBody_LegacyLoiter.label>
  <!-- EN: A first-generation pulsejet loitering munition in the spirit of the V-1, rail-launched and flown by a clockwork inertial autopilot along a preset heading, slow and easy to detect with accuracy measured in neighbourhoods but needing only steel, fuel and a simple jet tube to be thrown at a target beyond the horizon, with nothing to configure: it is built, loaded onto the rail, and fired. -->
  <DMSE_MissileBody_LegacyLoiter.description>TODO</DMSE_MissileBody_LegacyLoiter.description>
  <!-- EN: legacy interceptor loitering munition -->
  <DMSE_MissileBody_LegacyInterceptor.label>TODO</DMSE_MissileBody_LegacyInterceptor.label>
  <!-- EN: A first-generation guided interceptor loitering munition built around four oversized fins and a radio command link: it is launched to circle over the target area and only then dives on an incoming aircraft under an operator&apos;s command, slow, short-legged and only marginally accurate, yet a genuine guided interceptor in an age when anti-aircraft fire is still aimed by eye. It leaves the factory in a fixed configuration rather than being assembled per target. -->
  <DMSE_MissileBody_LegacyInterceptor.description>TODO</DMSE_MissileBody_LegacyInterceptor.description>
